NOTICE for the KAT audio in kat/audio and the data derived from it

The five clips clip_a_48k.wav, clip_b_48k_loss.wav, clip_c_24k.wav, clip_d_16k.wav and clip_f_32k.wav are derived works of
excerpts of the LibriSpeech corpus, test-clean subset (clip f is clip a resampled to 32 kHz, see below). Two more files, clip_g_16k.wav and
clip_i_16k.wav (KAT stage 13), are excerpts of the same corpus, unchanged except for the concatenation of consecutive utterances of one speaker
(speakers 5142 and 8230; the utterance ids are in kat/inputs/s13_sources.json):

  Vassil Panayotov, Guoguo Chen, Daniel Povey and Sanjeev Khudanpur,
  "LibriSpeech: an ASR corpus based on public domain audio books", ICASSP 2015.
  https://www.openslr.org/12/

LibriSpeech is derived from LibriVox audiobooks (public domain recordings) and is licensed under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes made to the original audio: excerpts of a few seconds taken from the listed utterances; sample-rate
conversion (to 48, 24, 32 and 16 kHz); added synthetic noise (low-level out-of-band noise above 8 kHz on the
48 kHz and 24 kHz clips, stationary white noise at about 12 dB signal-to-noise ratio on clip d); band limiting
to 3.8 kHz (clip c); level changes and hard clipping of one segment (clip c); simulated packet loss with crude
concealment (clip b); the first 6.75 s of clip a resampled to 32 kHz (4.5 s) with a handful of samples set to full-scale
extreme values (clip f). The source utterance ids and offsets are listed in audio_meta.json ("sources").
The clips are test vectors only; they are not recordings of the original speakers' intended speech.

The pseudo-random choices and the packet-loss and clipping metadata are recorded in audio_meta.json.

Derived data: kat/inputs/template_g.f32 (a speaker embedding computed from further utterances of speaker 5142), cohort.bin (80 speaker embeddings
computed from 4.096 s excerpts of the other 38 test-clean speakers) and the embeddings stored in the KAT stages 5, 6 and 13 are numerical
features computed from LibriSpeech excerpts with the CAM++ model; they contain no audio. The same attribution applies to them. The files
kat/inputs and cohort.bin were written by the generator that also writes the rest of the KAT.
